Plasmashell is the main Plasma desktop process handling panels, widgets, wallpaper, and the system tray.

@text
Restarting Plasmashell

Kill and restart the shell without logging out. Useful after config changes or when the desktop becomes unresponsive.

@code bash
# Restart plasmashell (Plasma 5/6)
kquitapp5 plasmashell || killall plasmashell
kstart5 plasmashell &

# Plasma 6 variant
kquitapp6 plasmashell || killall plasmashell
kstart plasmashell &

# Quick one-liner restart
plasmashell --replace &disown

@text
Virtual Desktops

Manage virtual desktops from the command line via D-Bus or qdbus.

@code bash
# List current virtual desktops (Plasma 5 — KWin D-Bus)
qdbus org.kde.KWin /VirtualDesktopManager org.kde.KWin.VirtualDesktopManager.desktops

# Get number of virtual desktops
qdbus org.kde.KWin /VirtualDesktopManager org.kde.KWin.VirtualDesktopManager.count

# Create a new virtual desktop (name, position)
qdbus org.kde.KWin /VirtualDesktopManager org.kde.KWin.VirtualDesktopManager.createDesktop 4 "Desktop 5"

# Remove a virtual desktop by ID
qdbus org.kde.KWin /VirtualDesktopManager org.kde.KWin.VirtualDesktopManager.removeDesktop "desktop-id"

# Switch to a specific desktop (1-indexed)
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin org.kde.KWin.setCurrentDesktop 2

# Get current desktop number
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin org.kde.KWin.currentDesktop

@text
Activities

Activities provide separate workspace contexts with independent widgets and wallpapers.

@code bash
# List activities
qdbus org.kde.ActivityManager /ActivityManager/Activities ListActivities

# Get current activity ID
qdbus org.kde.ActivityManager /ActivityManager/Activities CurrentActivity

# Create a new activity (returns ID)
qdbus org.kde.ActivityManager /ActivityManager/Activities AddActivity "Development"

# Switch to an activity by ID
qdbus org.kde.ActivityManager /ActivityManager/Activities SetCurrentActivity "activity-id"

# Stop an activity (unload from memory)
qdbus org.kde.ActivityManager /ActivityManager/Activities StopActivity "activity-id"

# Remove an activity
qdbus org.kde.ActivityManager /ActivityManager/Activities RemoveActivity "activity-id"

@text
Widgets (Plasmoids)

Manage desktop and panel widgets. Widgets can be added/removed via the GUI or scripting.

@code bash
# List installed widgets/plasmoids
plasmapkg2 -l --type plasmoid

# Install a plasmoid from file
plasmapkg2 -i /path/to/widget.plasmoid

# Remove an installed plasmoid
plasmapkg2 -r org.kde.plasma.widgetname

# Upgrade an installed plasmoid
plasmapkg2 -u /path/to/widget.plasmoid

# Plasma 6 uses kpackagetool6
kpackagetool6 -l --type Plasma/Applet
kpackagetool6 -i /path/to/widget.plasmoid

@text
Panel Management

Panels can be configured via D-Bus scripting or the interactive panel editor.

@code bash
# Open panel toolbox (right-click panel > "Enter Edit Mode")
# Programmatic panel creation via Plasma scripting console:
# Desktop right-click > Enter Edit Mode > Add Panel

# Launch the Plasma scripting console (for complex automation)
plasmawindowed org.kde.plasma.calculator   # test a widget standalone

# Lock/unlock widgets
qdbus org.kde.plasmashell /PlasmaShell org.kde.PlasmaShell.setDashboardShown false
